\ tools/dict-dump-addr.4 - dump every word in the dictionary, with
\ addresses, so a call target can be resolved.
\
\ Emits, for every word:
\     H <nfa> <raw count byte>
\     N <body-start> <body-end> <name>
\     B <addr> <value>          (one per body cell)
\
\ WHY THIS IS A TWO-PASS WALK. The word list is HASHED: 32 threads, each
\ a separate chain. Following one chain no longer visits every word and,
\ less obviously, no longer visits them in ADDRESS order either. Both
\ matter. The dump must be complete, and the layout pass downstream
\ derives a word's body END from where the NEXT word's link cell starts,
\ which is only the next word in the chain if the chain is in address
\ order. It used to be. It is not any more.
\
\ So: collect every nfa from every thread, sort by address descending,
\ and emit in that order. Descending, because the dump has always been
\ newest-first and tools/layout.py reverses it to recover definition
\ order.

BASE @ DECIMAL
VARIABLE NFA
VARIABLE BP
VARIABLE BE
VARIABLE NFATAB
VARIABLE #NFA
VARIABLE TA
: CELLB 1 CELLS ;

\ In a definition: ABORT" is compile-only, and interpreting it here
\ segfaulted before a single word was dumped.
: INIT-NFATAB 8192 CELLS ALLOCATE ABORT" dict-dump: out of memory" NFATAB ! ;
INIT-NFATAB

: COLLECT ( --- )
\ Every nfa in every thread, in whatever order the chains give them.
  0 #NFA !
  FORTH-WORDLIST @ 1+ 1 DO
    FORTH-WORDLIST I CELLS + @ NFA !
    BEGIN NFA @ WHILE
      NFA @ NFATAB @ #NFA @ CELLS + !
      1 #NFA +!
      NFA @ CELLB - DUP @ ?DUP IF + NFA ! ELSE DROP 0 NFA ! THEN
    REPEAT
  LOOP ;

: SWAPC ( a --- )
\ Exchange the cells at a and a+CELL.
  TA !
  TA @ @ TA @ CELLB + @
  TA @ ! TA @ CELLB + ! ;

: SORTNFA ( --- )
\ Descending by address. A bubble sort, because it runs once over a few
\ hundred entries and the clarity is worth more than the cycles.
  #NFA @ 1- 0 DO
    #NFA @ 1- 0 DO
      NFATAB @ I CELLS +
      DUP @ OVER CELLB + @ < IF SWAPC ELSE DROP THEN
    LOOP
  LOOP ;

: DUMP ( --- )
  COLLECT SORTNFA
  #NFA @ 0 DO
    NFATAB @ I CELLS + @ NFA !
    NFA @ DUP C@ 31 AND 1+ ALIGNED + BP !
    \ The body ends where the next word by ADDRESS begins its link cell.
    \ The newest word - first in this descending order - ends at HERE.
    I 0= IF HERE ELSE NFATAB @ I 1- CELLS + @ CELLB - THEN BE !
    \ The raw count byte carries flag bits above the length - bit 5 is
    \ the MACRO flag cross.4's PRIMITIVE sets. TYPE below masks them
    \ off, so without this line an image rebuilt from this dump would
    \ silently lose every flag.
    S" H " TYPE NFA @ . NFA @ C@ . CR
    S" N " TYPE BP @ . BE @ . NFA @ 1+ NFA @ C@ 31 AND TYPE CR
    BEGIN BP @ BE @ < WHILE
      S" B " TYPE BP @ . BP @ @ . CR
      BP @ CELLB + BP !
    REPEAT
  LOOP ;

\ The S line anchors every address above to an offset in the saved
\ image, which runs from START to HERE. Printed before DUMP runs, so
\ HERE is the value the dump itself will see - the nfa table is on the
\ HEAP, so it does not move HERE.
S" S " TYPE START @ . HERE . CR
DUMP
\ The prologue: the cells between START and the oldest word's link
\ cell. ip = base starts executing at offset 0, so the first two are
\ code and the image cannot be rebuilt without them. DUMP walks bodies
\ only and never sees this region.
\
\ This MUST be a definition. A DO/+LOOP typed at the interpreter runs
\ once and stops - the same interpret-mode hazard GOALS.md records for
\ IF/THEN in this kernel.
: PROLOGUE-DUMP
  START @ DUP 6 CELLS + SWAP DO
    S" P " TYPE I . I @ . CR
  1 CELLS +LOOP ;
PROLOGUE-DUMP
BASE ! BYE
